                                "sense_id": "54f69e52-4d96-38ad-b425-bdf0e8b618d5",
                                "text": "Fortunately, I come from a family that was well circumstanced."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2996ce6f-d1fd-4995-9bd7-8a704345c59a",
                                "sense_id": "54f69e52-4d96-38ad-b425-bdf0e8b618d5",
                                "text": "1886, Thomas Hardy, The Mayor of Casterbridge, Oxford World's Classics, Oxford University Press, 1987, Chapter XIV, p. 88,\nIt might have been supposed that, given a girl rapidly becoming good-looking, comfortably circumstanced, and for the first time in her life commanding ready money, she would go and make a fool of herself by dress."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
